; worldsave.eval — the world tier survives a save/load round trip (P2).
;
; The global tier is the half of the save that is NOT about any one dungeon:
; where the party is in the world, elapsed time, what it has discovered. This
; moves all three off their new-game values FIRST, because a round trip that
; starts from the defaults proves nothing — a save that wrote nothing at all
; would reproduce them exactly.
logecho on
reset

; --- off the defaults (new game leaves the party at the world start, 6,6) ---
worldpos 3 12
discover crypt_gate
world

; --- round trip -------------------------------------------------------------
save worldtrip
load worldtrip
world
